  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIt seems that many developers find it weird that the default behaviour of a <button> element is to submit the form when no type is specified. See this [SO question](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/932653/how-to-prevent-buttons-from-submitting-forms) as an illustration. Why not make the _missing value default_ of the type attribute be 'button' instead of 'submit' as I feel it is more logical with the very nature of the button element ?\r\n\r\nNow I appreciate that there is a backwards compatibility issue here, as it would break many websites which rely on the default submit behaviour, but medium to long term this makes more sense and is more consistent.\r\n\r\nSorry if this is a duplicate, I could not find any other one stating the same thing.",
